  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform chain of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> length is placed on a table such that a part of its length is hanging over the edge of the table. The system is at rest. The co-efficient of static friction between the chain and the surface of the table is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, the maximum length of the chain hanging from the table is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo></math>mass per unit length of the chain and length of mass hanging through the table is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5c95b8d9-a61b-4f07-a8b4-c84531504c0f-image.png\" style=\"width: 251px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>Normal force applied by the table on the chain will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>g</mi></math>.</p><p>Tension developed in the chain will balance the gravitational force acting in the downward direction,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>g</mi></math>.</p><p>Maximum limiting force possible for the part of the table,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p>For equilibrium,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>g</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
